<title>GERMANY: German labour market remains weak - Jagoda.</title>
<headline>German labour market remains weak - Jagoda.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>German labour market weakness was little changed in August, Federal Labour Office President Bernhard Jagoda said.</p>
<p>While the seasonally adjusted number of unemployed showed a small 14,000 rise to 3.939 million, the unadjusted number declined by 10,000 to 3.902 million.</p>
<p>&quot;The decline was limited to east Germany, where vacations have ended,&quot; Jagoda said. &quot;Nothing has changed in the economically subdued development and the structural burdens.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
